  "notes": "min_2a_mod_3n is the closest approach to 0 of the orbit of 2 in Z/3^n, taking the signed-magnitude representative in [-3^n/2, 3^n/2]. A 'sum-product' / mixing assumption would predict this is comparable to the trivial pigeonhole bound 3^n / |O| = 3^n / (2*3^{n-1}) = 3/2; the data shows the orbit in fact achieves values within an order of magnitude of that, which is the OPPOSITE of what would help cycles (the orbit is TOO well-distributed). See sum_product_markoff.md for interpretation."
